// TEST: anticomm on a function declaration, false only on the diagonal (rejects)
// ERROR: BL4013
// ERROR-CONTAINS: at x = y = 2 the body is -1, not 0
// The declaration seam runs the same witness as the lambda seam (080): the
// sign law holds off the diagonal, but g(a, a) = -1, and strict storage would
// answer every diagonal read with 0. Integer kernel: the value is exact.
function g(x: Int64, y: Int64) where anticomm(x, y) -> Int64 = if x > y then 1 else -1
